WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.843 --> 00:00:09.453
This page explains how the whole site works. The panel you are reading now appears on every page, always tuned to that page.

2
00:00:09.453 --> 00:00:20.460
Read the success guide first. Five habits for doing an asynchronous course well: plan your times, learn from the experience, quiz yourself honestly, have a plan for being stuck, and keep your own evidence.

3
00:00:20.461 --> 00:00:31.493
Skim the cards in order. They cover privacy, copyright, translation, accessibility, and the site's known limits, including that saved work lives only in this browser.

4
00:00:31.493 --> 00:00:42.498
Use the diagram to keep this site and Blackboard straight. You learn and practise here. You submit, discuss, and get grades on Blackboard. If the two ever disagree, Blackboard wins.

5
00:00:42.498 --> 00:00:53.503
Look for the How to use this page bar anywhere you go. Every page carries its own version of this panel with steps for that page. Open it whenever a page feels unfamiliar.

6
00:00:53.503 --> 00:01:04.504
Report anything broken. The report button opens your own email with the page details filled in. You add what happened and press send. Nothing is collected by this site.

7
00:01:04.504 --> 00:01:15.514
Use Clear my saved work on a shared computer. It removes every note, answer, and setting this site has saved in this browser. Download your weekly notes first if you want to keep them.

8
00:01:15.515 --> 00:01:26.520
Back up your saved work. The Take your saved work with you box on this page downloads everything you have typed and rated as one file, and restores it on any device. The accessibility statement lives here too.

9
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:32.055
Nothing on this site is graded. Blackboard is the only official gradebook.

10
00:01:32.055 --> 00:01:36.270
Where next: Head back Home and open the current week.
